adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts` the webhook authentication check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset (i.e., `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET === undefined`), and the request does not include the header (so `req.headers[...] === undefined`), the comparison evaluates to `false` and the request is incorrectly allowed to proceed. This creates a real security bypass when the secret is not configured, which is plausible given `.env.example` sets `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""` and deploys often start with missing env vars.
